  "fold_composition_paragraph": "Standard stratified 5-fold CV (stratified on cancer type) already approximates center balance closely: per-fold center shares deviate from the global center distribution by at most 0.85pp (mean 0.29pp), because sequencing centers are nearly confounded with cancer types (15 of 20 types are sequenced essentially at a single center), so stratifying on type implicitly stratifies on center. The center-stratified scheme (within each type, folds stratified on center) tightens this about 8-fold, to at most 0.11pp (mean 0.06pp). The reviewer's concern is therefore half right: center stratification perturbs fold composition only modestly in absolute terms, so the center-stratified CV test has limited power by construction and the unchanged Bio MAF-vs-burden gap (0.502 vs 0.497) should not carry the batch-effect argument alone. It remains one of four converging lines: the winner's top-50 carries no significant excess center variance (p=0.11), cross-center OVR transfer holds at 0.77-0.94 AUROC where testable, and the frozen model transfers to the independent PCAWG consortium cohort.",
  "elapsed_minutes": 9.3,
  "key_limitation": "Cross-center testing is only feasible for 5 of 20 types (CESC, OV, KIRP, KIRC, COAD); the other 15 types have <10 samples at a second center, so no train->test center pair can be formed. The 0.77-0.94 AUROC range therefore describes the testable subset, not all 20 types."
 },
